From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000010 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NixOS module overlay <noreply@example.com>
Date: Fri, 28 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 10/10] Create the fulltext index with one typeless PUT

misc/elasticsearch/bin/init cannot create item_fulltext_index on a
self-hosted OpenSearch deployment. Three separate reasons:

  - It curls -d @init.json and, via bin/update-settings, -d
    @settings.json. Neither file exists: the repo ships them as
    init.json-sample and settings.json-sample, expecting an operator to
    copy them first. On a fresh checkout curl fails on the missing file.

  - Its last step is PUT /item_fulltext_index/item_fulltext/_mapping.
    Mapping types were removed in OpenSearch 2 / Elasticsearch 8, so
    that URL has no route and answers 400 "no handler found for uri" --
    the same fault patch 0009 fixes on the search side.

  - init.json-sample sets number_of_replicas: 1, which leaves a
    single-node cluster permanently yellow because the replica shard can
    never be allocated.

Collapse all of it into one typeless PUT with settings and mapping
inlined, so the script works against a stock single-node cluster with no
operator-supplied files. The mapping loses its "item_fulltext" wrapper
because a typeless mapping has no type key to wrap it in.

Without this the index simply does not exist, and a well-formed search
answers index_not_found_exception rather than returning results. Run
once per deployment:

    misc/elasticsearch/bin/init 127.0.0.1
---
diff --git a/misc/elasticsearch/bin/init b/misc/elasticsearch/bin/init
index 1234567..89abcde 100755
--- a/misc/elasticsearch/bin/init
+++ b/misc/elasticsearch/bin/init
@@ -13,9 +13,36 @@ HOST="$1"
 ITEM_FULLTEXT_DIR=$DIR/item_fulltext
 
-curl -XPUT "http://$HOST:9200/item_fulltext_index" -H "Content-Type: application/json" -d @$ITEM_FULLTEXT_DIR/init.json
-echo
-
-$DIR/bin/update-settings $HOST
-
-curl -XPUT "http://$HOST:9200/item_fulltext_index/item_fulltext/_mapping" -H "Content-Type: application/json" -d @$ITEM_FULLTEXT_DIR/mapping.json
-echo
+# Self-hosted: create the index in a single typeless PUT.
+#
+# The upstream flow does not work here for three reasons:
+#   - it reads init.json / settings.json, which ship only as
+#     *.json-sample, so curl -d @... fails on a fresh checkout;
+#   - its mapping PUT names a type (/item_fulltext_index/
+#     item_fulltext/_mapping), and mapping types were removed in
+#     OpenSearch 2 / Elasticsearch 8 -- no route, 400;
+#   - number_of_replicas: 1 leaves a single-node cluster yellow
+#     forever, since the replica can never be allocated.
+#
+# Settings and mapping are inlined so this runs against a stock
+# cluster with no operator-supplied files. Mapping is unwrapped:
+# typeless mappings have no type key.
+curl -XPUT "http://$HOST:9200/item_fulltext_index" -H "Content-Type: application/json" -d @- <<'JSON'
+{
+	"settings": {
+		"number_of_shards": 1,
+		"number_of_replicas": 0,
+		"refresh_interval": "5s",
+		"query.default_field": "content"
+	},
+	"mappings": {
+		"_source": { "enabled": false },
+		"_routing": { "required": true },
+		"dynamic": false,
+		"properties": {
+			"libraryID": { "type": "integer" },
+			"content": { "type": "text" }
+		}
+	}
+}
+JSON
+echo
